WebKit: the PlayStation page events carry text, modifiers, time and the held button.

WKPageHandleKeyboardEvent, WKPageHandleMouseEvent and WKPageHandleWheelEvent are the
C API a UI process sends input through (the PlayStation port's, which the LazyOS UI
process uses). As shipped they drop what a window system tells them:

 * keyboard: the text of the key was always "", so a character never reached a text
   field (the factory takes a null string to mean "what the key code stands for", and
   an empty one for "types nothing"); now WKKeyboardEvent.text is passed, null when the
   key has none. The modifiers (TODO in the source) are translated from
   WKEventModifiers to libwpe's bits;
 * mouse: the time was always 0, so WebKit's double-click detection (a time and a
   distance) counted every click at one spot as one more click of a series; now it is
   the monotonic clock. A move with a button held names that button in the modifiers,
   which is how WebKit knows a drag (text selection), and a press has its button down;
 * wheel: both axes were always sent, and WebKit takes only the sign of an axis event,
   so a zero scrolled one line to the right on every vertical step; now only an axis
   that moved is sent, with the modifiers.

